From d124d2a9caeabd0ac528de30f3572d04ec7559eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (for Jeremy Rabin)" <jeremybrandonrabin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:08:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Trusted connector relay, dead-token detection + Reconnect,
 weekday schedules

- talk_to_operator via a connector token now reaches the operator as [OWNER via connector "<label>"]; system prompt rule 9 (CHANNELS) tells operators a connector token IS the owner's authorisation, so no more "unverified relay" refusals.
- connections.js: a failed refresh (invalid_grant / expired / revoked) flags the connection needsReauth once, logs it to activity, and returns a plain "owner must reconnect X in Settings > Connections" error instead of retrying; reconnecting clears the flag. Twice-daily token sweep surfaces dead tokens before an operator hits them. UI shows a red "needs reconnect" pill and a Reconnect button. list_connections (MCP) and /api/connections expose status.
- schedules: optional days[] (0=Sun..6=Sat, UTC) on POST /api/schedules and MCP add_schedule; list_schedules shows days.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018kcCA1ESAHa7LVFQZh8nah
